Adapt RDO's rpm-master openstack-nova.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(nova 33.0.2).

The same upstream change as keystone and placement, now in nova: the generated
WSGI scripts are gone. nova 33.0.2's pyproject.toml declares eleven console
scripts and none of them is an API server -

    nova-compute, nova-conductor, nova-manage, nova-novncproxy, nova-policy,
    nova-rootwrap, nova-rootwrap-daemon, nova-scheduler, nova-serialproxy,
    nova-spicehtml5proxy, nova-status

- while the API is now importable at nova/wsgi/osapi_compute.py and
  nova/wsgi/metadata.py. Without this the build dies at the end of %install:

    error: File not found: .../usr/bin/nova-api*
    error: File not found: .../usr/bin/nova-metadata-wsgi

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT FIX, because it is a deployment decision
and not a packaging one: the distgit also ships

    openstack-nova-api.service          ExecStart=/usr/bin/nova-api
    openstack-nova-metadata-api.service ExecStart=/usr/bin/nova-api-metadata
    openstack-nova-os-compute-api.service

and all three now point at binaries that do not exist. On 2026.1 the Nova API
has to be run as a WSGI application - mod_wsgi or uwsgi against
nova.wsgi.osapi_compute and nova.wsgi.metadata. That is the same shape Ubuntu
26.04 already uses (nova-api is an Apache vhost there, with no unit), so a
Rocky hagistack would write its own httpd configuration rather than enable
these units. Leaving them visibly dead is more honest than pointing them at
something invented here.

diff -ur a/nova/openstack-nova.spec b/nova/openstack-nova.spec
--- a/openstack-nova.spec	2026-09-28 21:43:17
+++ b/openstack-nova.spec	2026-09-28 22:37:47
@@ -620,8 +620,6 @@
 %{_unitdir}/openstack-nova-scheduler.service
 
 %files api
-%{_bindir}/nova-api*
-%{_bindir}/nova-metadata-wsgi
 %{_unitdir}/openstack-nova-*api.service
 
 %files conductor
